# MCP-first guardrail -- PreToolUse(Grep) hook. Injects a reminder as additionalContext; never blocks.
# ASCII only (PowerShell 5.1 reads .ps1 as ANSI); English text avoids encoding pitfalls.
Write-Output '{"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"PreToolUse","additionalContext":"[MCP-first guardrail] Locate/analyze code -> query platform MCP FIRST, do not grep-first. symbols/defs/call-chains/impact: codegraph (codegraph_search/context/callers/callees/impact/node). cross-layer/table-usage/endpoint-callers/page-deps/business-domain: graph (find_table_usage/find_api_callers/find_impact/find_node_domain/search_nodes). rules/design/incident docs: platform-docs (search_docs/get_by_file). grep+Read ONLY for 4 fallbacks: dirty worktree in query scope / stale index / MCP unavailable / verify real line numbers after edits. Confirm this grep is a fallback, else switch to MCP."}}'
